Being an experienced player (although I'm posting for the first time), I'd say
you should wish for any of the "best" items that you don't have and are rare to
find. By "best", I mean the best armor for each armor slot, and some valuable
and rare tools. These are:

helm of telepathy
gauntlets of dexterity
water walking boots / speed boots
shield of reflection
Hawaiaan shirt

(No point in wishing for GDSM, since you can get it from the dragon if you
have a want of polymorph. Also, it's relatively easy to find a cloak of 
displacement).

Useful tools/other stuff that you can wish for : blessed luckstone, magic marker,
blindfold, stethoscope, amulets of life saving.

On early experience levels a ring of levitation/conflict or gauntlets of
power are useful. Depending on what you find on your way, you may need to
wish for some other items if you are unlucky, such as a ring of protection
from shape changers (indispensable on later levels).

Never wish for a scroll. Wish for a magic marker instead, and write on your
useless scrolls after you make them blank; you can get much more scrolls
that way than directly wishing for them. The one exception is if you need
a type of scroll and you haven't found any, it is rare, and you are not a
wizard (this really applies only to the genocide and charging scrolls).

You can also wish for blessed potions of gain ability, but do that only if
your intelligence and/or dexterity is low; the other stats can be raised in
other ways. Note that this will lead you to be able to raise your HPs and
level much easier than summoning nurses/wraiths, so there is no point in
wishing for cursed scrolls of genocide.

Answering your side question 1 : No, genociding liches will still leave you
exposed to level drain attacks. This is the point that many posters miss
when they compare the various weapons and say things such as "Frosty is the
best" or "for later levels, go for Mjollnir". The truth is that when you
have a decent number of HPs and good level/stats, you don't really care
for the difference in damage, but you do care for keeping your level intact
(unless you want to go raising it every so often). There are only two
things that can protect you from level drain attacks, and that is wielding
Excalibur or Stormy. Now, you can get Excalibur easily (and rustfree), and
you don't want the level drain attack of Stormy on lower levels (to be able
to get these intrinsics) and you don't care about it on higher levels. So
the weapon of choice is Excalibur, and there is no need to wish for it.

Side question 2 : No, you can't group amulets together, therefore you can't
wish for more than one.

BTW, you have two more wishes, after you recharge your two magic lamps.


